  "assessment": {
    "p95": "Public main p95: 66.6ms, 66.7ms, 66.7ms. Candidate p95: 50.0ms, 50.1ms, 66.7ms; medians 66.7ms vs 50.1ms. Two candidate repeats are lower and one ties; three coarse browser samples do not establish a broad mobile-performance pass.",
    "throughput": "All nine patterns remain active. Native projectile-array admissions confirm 26 awakened shots on public main and 76 on the candidate (2.92x). This isolated fixture holds boss awakening for the whole sequence; it does not represent naturally timed awakenings. Candidate p95 remains far above a 16.7ms 60fps budget.",
    "renderingCosts": "The baseline self-blits the stage canvas 464 times (178 grayscale); candidate self-blits are 0. Wrapped persona-sprite drawImage calls rise from 3177 to 27729 as projectile volume increases. Thus the measured improvement is removal of expensive whole-canvas grayscale self-blits, not a reduction in all rendering work.",
    "bitmapContactCache": "Candidate repeats recorded 4,330–17,355 stable persona-shape reuses and 61–84 misses. All candidate runs reported every image decoded and zero missing contact plans; misses are shape-cache misses, not missing files.",
    "physicalDevices": "Not tested.",
    "legacyComparison": "The older 9463d5 runtime is excluded from barrage-performance attribution. Movement is checked separately by tests/rc142-movement-space-browser.cjs across 55 maps, two modes, four arena edges, and three browser layouts.",
    "cpuThrottle4x": "Two matched full-sequence repeats per runtime. Baseline p95 250/250ms; candidate p95 266.6/283.3ms, with 26 vs 76 actual projectile admissions. Candidate median intervals were lower, but p95 tails were about 7–13% slower. Both builds have severe frame pacing under this emulation (max 467–667ms); do not claim a general mobile win.",
    "followupRendererOptimization": "The RC142 direct drawImage wrapper preserves native emitted shots and exact drawImage arguments. At CPU 1×, three repeats show unchanged rounded p50/p95 medians. At CPU 4×, two repeats show lower median p50 (183.3→174.9ms) and p95 (258.35→241.75ms), with effectively unchanged median maximum (~516.7ms). This is a small emulator-only result; drawImage remains the largest CPU profile bucket and intervals remain far beyond 16.7ms."
  },
